{"id":"f79c62ae79f22e6f","group":"58","path":"58/batch07/58-df-zfc-set11-closure-under-ordered-pairs.md","title":"ZFC Set11 Closure Under Ordered Pairs","display":"df-zfc-set11-closure-under-ordered-pairs — ZFC Set11 Closure Under Ordered Pairs","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-zfc-set11-closure-under-ordered-pairs","aliases":["58-df-zfc-set11-closure-under-ordered-pairs"],"display":"df-zfc-set11-closure-under-ordered-pairs — ZFC Set11 Closure Under Ordered Pairs","depends_on":["[[../batch14/58-df-zfc-set-ordered-pair.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-zfc-set11-closure-under-ordered-pairs"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-zfc-set11-closure-under-ordered-pairs</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-zfc-set11-closure-under-ordered-pairs — ZFC Set11 Closure Under Ordered Pairs"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"599d16bb1d9ed41c\" href=\"?note=599d16bb1d9ed41c\" title=\"../batch14/58-df-zfc-set-ordered-pair.md\">../batch14/58-df-zfc-set-ordered-pair.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"H,x,y,p\\in V\">\\(H,x,y,p\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcSetOrderedPair}_S(p,x,y)\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcSetOrderedPair}_S(p,x,y)\\)</span> (Kuratowski ordered-pair predicate)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcSet11ClosureUnderOrderedPairs}_S(H)\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcSet11ClosureUnderOrderedPairs}_S(H)\\)</span> (predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}set11\\text{-}closure\\text{-}under\\text{-}ordered\\text{-}pairs} \\vdash \\mathrm{ZfcSet11ClosureUnderOrderedPairs}_S(H)\\leftrightarrow \\forall x,y\\in H\\;\\exists p\\in H\\;\\mathrm{ZfcSetOrderedPair}_S(p,x,y)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}set11\\text{-}closure\\text{-}under\\text{-}ordered\\text{-}pairs} \\vdash \\mathrm{ZfcSet11ClosureUnderOrderedPairs}_S(H)\\leftrightarrow \\forall x,y\\in H\\;\\exists p\\in H\\;\\mathrm{ZfcSetOrderedPair}_S(p,x,y)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Closure is tied to the canonical Kuratowski ordered-pair code rather than an unregistered bracket notation; uniqueness of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"p\">\\(p\\)</span> follows from that upstream definition.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch14/58-df-zfc-set-ordered-pair.md","status":"resolved","id":"599d16bb1d9ed41c","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch14/58-df-zfc-set-ordered-pair.md]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"H,x,y,p\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ZfcSetOrderedPair}_S(p,x,y)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ZfcSet11ClosureUnderOrderedPairs}_S(H)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}set11\\text{-}closure\\text{-}under\\text{-}ordered\\text{-}pairs} \\vdash \\mathrm{ZfcSet11ClosureUnderOrderedPairs}_S(H)\\leftrightarrow \\forall x,y\\in H\\;\\exists p\\in H\\;\\mathrm{ZfcSetOrderedPair}_S(p,x,y)","display":true},{"tex":"p","display":false}],"bytes":1035,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-3400","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch07/58-df-zfc-set11-closure-under-ordered-pairs.md|58-df-zfc-set11-closure-under-ordered-pairs]]（batch07）"}],"outgoing":["599d16bb1d9ed41c"]}